{
 "result": "fibmod.py is done. It reduces n mod P = 2(10^9+7+1), since the Pisano period of 1e9+7 divides P, so the fast-doubling loop runs about 31 iterations instead of about 60. It also caches repeated inputs and reads stdin in one pass. It matches the public sample (in-0 to out-0, fib(10)=55) byte for byte. A variant with these changes scored 4.642 against 2.609 for the previous body (+78%) and was adopted. Only one sample was checked, so the remaining samples are untested.",
